The funnel compares separate groups; it is not a conversion process. Any percentage labels should not be interpreted as user drop-off or movement between classes. Higher battery drain also does not establish that a device has worse battery life, because users may have different usage patterns.
## Font Pattern, Colours and Dashboard Formatting

- **Primary chosen font:** Times New Roman, explicitly applied to main headings, visual titles, and many axes, legends and slicer labels. Some elements retain inherited/default formatting; the file does not establish that every text element uses the same font.
- **Main headings:** large, bold and centered. Dashboard 1's main heading is explicitly set to 60 pt.
- **Visual titles:** bold, commonly around 17–19 pt where explicitly configured; many Dashboard 2 and 3 titles use 18 pt.
- **Axes and labels:** smaller text, frequently around 11–13 pt where configured, so values remain distinguishable from titles.
- **Number formatting:** generally two decimals for usage averages; a whole-number display for average installed apps.
- **Colour pattern:** orange/peach for Dashboard 1, purple/lavender for Dashboard 2, and pink/rose for Dashboard 3.
- **Layout:** prominent page heading, grouped summary values, comparison charts and a page-specific slicer. Generated layout images were design references, not analytical outputs.

## Supporting Chart Pages

The saved file also contains **Cards & KPI**, **Donut chart**, **Bar chart**, **Column chart**, **Treemap**, **Line Chart**, **Scatter plot** and **Funnel chart** pages. These retain individual visuals used during report development. The three numbered dashboard pages are the main presentation pages.
